// EXPECT: the return clause of 'grow' narrows word to int; declare a int local, assign it, and return that
// IDCPY-ACCEPTS
// docs/SPEC.md 1. The return clause used to narrow silently -- idem's engine
// relied on it as a way to narrow without spending an action -- but that made
// it the one place in the language where a narrowing conversion went
// unwritten. idc.py has no rule against this: it compiles the program and
// returns the truncated value.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  word a = 4294967297;
  int b = grow(a);
  print(b);
} return int 0;

grow(word w) {
} return int w;
